    "title": "San Diego FC vs. Real Salt Lake Lineups, Head-to-Head Stats, Live Score & MLS Results",
    "text": "(Photo by San Diego FC&sol;MLS via Getty Images)San Diego FC hosts Real Salt Lake this Sunday, March 22, at Snapdragon Stadium at 4 p.m. PT, 7 p.m. ET, for the fifth round of MLS.Mikey Varas’ team is currently in fourth place in the Western Conference with 10 points after four matches and a record of three wins and one draw.AdvertisementReal Salt Lake, meanwhile, is in seventh place with nine points after four matches and a record of three wins and one loss.San Diego FC was eliminated from the Concacaf Champions Cup on Wednesday after losing 4-0 to Toluca at Estadio Nemesio Diez.The Californian club had won the first leg 3-2 on Wednesday, March 11, with a brace from David Vazquez and another goal from Anders Dreyer. However, they could not get past the Liga MX side.Real Salt Lake, for its part, won 2-1 in its most recent match against Austin FC last weekend, with an own goal from Oleksandr Svatok and a goal from Stijn Spierings.AdvertisementHere is all the key pre-match information, including how and where to watch live, predicted lineups, head-to-head stats, live score, and results.San Diego FC2Ingvartsen (27'), Dreyer (56')Real Salt Lake2Solans (17'), Olatunji (85')Confirmed Lineups for San Diego FC and Real Salt LakeSan Diego FCGoalkeeper: Ferree.Defenders: Bombino, Duah, McVey, Verhoeven.Midfielders: Tverskov, Valakari.Forwards: Vazquez, Pellegrino, Ingvartsen, Dreyer.Real Salt LakeGoalkeeper: Cabral.Defenders: Sanabria, Engel, Glad, Quinton, Gozo.Midfielders: Guilavogui, Dillon, Caliskan, Hezarkhani.Forwards: Solans.San Diego FC vs. Real Salt Lake Head-to-Head Stats & ResultsSan Diego FC and Real Salt Lake have met twice, according to FotMob, with San Diego FC winning once and Real Salt Lake once.The match endend with a 2-2 draw, with goals from Ingvartsen (27'), Dreyer (56'), Solans (17'), and Olatunji (85').AdvertisementThis story was originally published by Athlon Sports on Mar 22, 2026, where it first appeared in the Soccer section. Add Athlon 